<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>救生艇新闻：博客——保护人类</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/</link><description></description><lastBuildDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:26:06 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>现实没有基础——卡洛·罗维利</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/reality-has-no-foundation-carlo-rovelli</link><description>&lt;img src="https://politepaul.com/fd/dtDF30237DhP.xml" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:26:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/reality-has-no-foundation-carlo-rovelli</guid></item><item><title>人脑中的一个基因突变为病毒——科学家们不知道它在那里做什么</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/a-gene-from-the-human-brain-leapt-into-a-virus-and-scientists-have-no-idea-what-its-doing-there</link><description>研究人员称BC200的双重生命以前从未见过。其影响并不令人欣慰。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/a-gene-from-the-human-brain-leapt-into-a-virus-and-scientists-have-no-idea-what-its-doing-there.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:11:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/a-gene-from-the-human-brain-leapt-into-a-virus-and-scientists-have-no-idea-what-its-doing-there</guid></item><item><title>X 和 Y 染色体作为衰老和疾病的决定因素</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/x-and-y-chromosomes-as-determinants-of-aging-and-disease</link><description>传统上，性别差异被归因于性腺激素，但越来越多的证据表明，性染色体对健康、衰老和疾病发挥着独特的、细胞自主的影响。 XX 和 XY 补体改变基因剂量、表观遗传编程、免疫信号、新陈代谢和细胞应激反应，从而塑造女性和男性的衰老和疾病轨迹。这篇综述将性染色体生物学的机制进展（包括逃避 X 染色体失活、X 重新激活、X 起源亲本、X 偏斜、X 和 Y 连锁基因功能以及 Y 缺失）与衰老、神经系统疾病、免疫、癌症和心脏代谢疾病结合起来。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/x-and-y-chromosomes-as-determinants-of-aging-and-disease2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:56:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/x-and-y-chromosomes-as-determinants-of-aging-and-disease</guid></item><item><title>科学家可能发现了慢性疲劳的“统一理论”</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/scientists-may-have-found-a-unifying-theory-of-chronic-fatigue</link><description>科学家发现，五种看似无关的病症，包括长新冠、ME/CFS 和 PTSD，可能会破坏许多涉及免疫、新陈代谢和细胞能量的相同生物网络。这些发现可能有助于解释他们共同的症状，并可能为新的血液检测和治疗打开大门。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/scientists-may-have-found-a-unifying-theory-of-chronic-fatigue.webp" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:41:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/scientists-may-have-found-a-unifying-theory-of-chronic-fatigue</guid></item><item><title>人类文明能发展到多大？</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/how-big-could-human-civilization-get</link><description>&lt;img src="https://politepaul.com/fd/dtDF30237DhP.xml" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:26:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/how-big-could-human-civilization-get</guid></item><item><title>银河系中心的文明：在银河系最极端的能量场中蓬勃发展</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/civilizations-at-the-galactic-center-thriving-in-the-most-extreme-energy-fields-of-the-milky-way</link><description>&lt;img src="https://politepaul.com/fd/dtDF30237DhP.xml" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:11:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/civilizations-at-the-galactic-center-thriving-in-the-most-extreme-energy-fields-of-the-milky-way</guid></item><item><title>科幻作家 PJ Manney 谈新神话和科学</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/scifi-author-pj-manney-on-the-new-mythos-and-conscience</link><description>&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/scifi-author-pj-manney-on-the-new-mythos-and-conscience.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:53:22 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/scifi-author-pj-manney-on-the-new-mythos-and-conscience<